1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,657
Lesson 3.3.3: Lifestyle Modifications.

2
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:14,875
The lifestyle modifications section answers three questions about the patient.

3
00:00:14,925 --> 00:00:17,746
First, what type of diet the patient follows.

4
00:00:17,796 --> 00:00:19,663
Second, whether the patient sticks to it.

5
00:00:19,703 --> 00:00:23,197
Three places in PointClickCare tell us that.

6
00:00:23,247 --> 00:00:26,221
And third, whether the patient takes part in any therapy.

7
00:00:26,261 --> 00:00:31,214
Physical and occupational therapy are checked for every patient.

8
00:00:31,264 --> 00:00:36,256
Respiratory therapy only matters when the CCM condition is respiratory,

9
00:00:36,296 --> 00:00:40,055
such as COPD, emphysema or asthma.

10
00:00:40,105 --> 00:00:44,167
And speech therapy only when the CCM condition is psychiatric.

11
00:00:44,207 --> 00:00:49,676
For our patient, with hyperlipidemia, that leaves PT and OT.

12
00:00:50,933 --> 00:00:54,959
So far, our problem note covers the condition, its medications,

13
00:00:54,999 --> 00:00:58,338
and whether the patient takes them as prescribed.

14
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:01,826
Next comes Lifestyle Modifications: the patient's diet,

15
00:01:01,866 --> 00:01:06,029
whether they stick to it, and any therapy they take part in.

16
00:01:10,433 --> 00:01:13,960
The diet type is in the patient's profile in PointClickCare,

17
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,720
in the outline at the top of the page.

18
00:01:18,130 --> 00:01:22,618
Switching the outline to Expanded opens up the patient's full details.

19
00:01:24,267 --> 00:01:27,636
And there's the diet: no added salt, regular texture,

20
00:01:27,676 --> 00:01:30,632
and standard thin liquids consistency.

21
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:35,890
It goes into the note exactly as it's written here.

22
00:01:38,767 --> 00:01:42,968
If the outline doesn't show a diet, the Orders tab always has it.

23
00:01:46,767 --> 00:01:51,201
In Display Filters, we untick every order category except Diet.

24
00:01:52,867 --> 00:01:57,864
Searching then lists only the diet order, and it says exactly the same thing.

25
00:02:02,867 --> 00:02:03,880
Next question:

26
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:09,480
does the patient actually stick to this diet? The Tasks tab is the first place to look.

27
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:17,110
It lists the patient's daily care tasks, like bathing, dressing and eating.

28
00:02:18,070 --> 00:02:19,507
Eating is the one we need,

29
00:02:19,547 --> 00:02:23,542
and the question mark beside it opens its full history.

30
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:29,682
This report records every meal, with one row for each date and time.

31
00:02:31,867 --> 00:02:33,806
Only the last three columns matter here:

32
00:02:33,846 --> 00:02:38,601
Resident Not Available, Resident Refused, and Not Applicable.

33
00:02:38,667 --> 00:02:42,814
A mark in any of them means the patient missed a meal for that reason.

34
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:49,279
So we check the whole month, row by row.

35
00:02:52,733 --> 00:02:54,818
Here, all three columns stay empty:

36
00:02:54,858 --> 00:02:58,378
the patient didn't refuse or miss a single meal.

37
00:03:04,675 --> 00:03:07,723
The Assessments tab is the second place to check.

38
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:15,247
With the status and type filters on All,

39
00:03:15,287 --> 00:03:20,238
View All lists every assessment, up to 1500 of them.

40
00:03:25,633 --> 00:03:29,013
Searching for nutrition finds the Nutritional Assessment,

41
00:03:29,053 --> 00:03:32,881
completed on November 10, 2026.

42
00:03:43,067 --> 00:03:47,745
Inside, only one answer matters to us: the intake observation.

43
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:51,971
Here, the patient's oral intake is 76 to 100 percent,

44
00:03:52,011 --> 00:03:54,025
so the patient is adherent.

45
00:03:55,167 --> 00:04:00,493
The patient is non-adherent only if this answer says the patient refuses meals.

46
00:04:05,533 --> 00:04:07,892
The progress notes are the third place.

47
00:04:11,133 --> 00:04:14,722
On the Progress Notes tab, View All with a custom date range:

48
00:04:14,762 --> 00:04:18,068
for this scratch patient, the last 30 days.

49
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:27,843
A keyword search then does the work.

50
00:04:27,883 --> 00:04:32,156
Diet finds lines like: provide diet as ordered.

51
00:04:37,533 --> 00:04:42,524
Meals finds that the resident consumes more than 75 percent of meals.

52
00:04:44,733 --> 00:04:49,399
And nutrition finds the goal to maintain or improve nutritional status,

53
00:04:49,439 --> 00:04:52,227
with no new signs of malnutrition.

54
00:04:54,433 --> 00:04:58,189
What we're looking for is any sign that the patient refuses meals,

55
00:04:58,229 --> 00:05:03,304
or refuses the type of diet ordered, like a low sodium diet.

56
00:05:04,433 --> 00:05:09,351
Putting it all together: a missed meal in Tasks, a refusal in the progress notes,

57
00:05:09,391 --> 00:05:13,937
or poor intake in the assessment makes the patient non-adherent.

58
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,186
None of that turned up here,

59
00:05:16,226 --> 00:05:19,633
so the note says the patient is adherent to the diet.

60
00:05:22,367 --> 00:05:26,006
The last part of lifestyle modifications is therapy.

61
00:05:31,133 --> 00:05:36,258
Care Profile, right under the patient's photo, opens the patient's care profile.

62
00:05:40,033 --> 00:05:41,954
Its Therapies section lists physical,

63
00:05:41,994 --> 00:05:45,553
occupational, respiratory and speech therapy.

64
00:05:45,603 --> 00:05:49,687
None of them is checked, so the patient isn't receiving any therapy.

65
00:05:54,533 --> 00:05:57,572
With hyperlipidemia as the CCM condition,

66
00:05:57,612 --> 00:06:01,932
physical and occupational therapy are the ones that count.

67
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:08,154
So the note says: not participating in PT or OT.

68
00:06:12,133 --> 00:06:14,154
The Orders tab confirms it.

69
00:06:17,933 --> 00:06:20,032
Therapy orders aren't pharmacy, diet,

70
00:06:20,072 --> 00:06:24,781
lab or supplement orders, so in the filters we keep only Other.

71
00:06:26,433 --> 00:06:30,300
Searching shows no order for physical or occupational therapy,

72
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:32,463
which matches the care profile.

73
00:06:38,633 --> 00:06:42,681
To wrap up: the diet type comes from the expanded profile outline,

74
00:06:42,721 --> 00:06:44,871
or from the diet order.

75
00:06:44,921 --> 00:06:46,453
Adherence starts in Tasks,

76
00:06:46,493 --> 00:06:50,505
where the eating history shows any refused or missed meals.

77
00:06:50,555 --> 00:06:56,117
The nutritional assessment's intake observation confirms how much the patient eats.

78
00:06:56,167 --> 00:07:00,059
A keyword search of the progress notes catches any refusal of meals

79
00:07:00,099 --> 00:07:01,868
or of the diet type.

80
00:07:01,918 --> 00:07:06,407
And therapy comes from the Care Profile, confirmed by the Other orders.

81
00:07:08,567 --> 00:07:11,664
Next, we trend the patient's labs and vitals.
